      "en": "What a nut job.",
      "zh": "真是个疯子。"
    },
    {
      "id": 114,
      "start": 278.86,
      "end": 279.62,
      "en": "He's a nut job.",
      "zh": "他是个疯子。"
    },
    {
      "id": 115,
      "start": 280.04,
      "end": 280.44,
      "en": "Okay.",
      "zh": "好的。"
    },
    {
      "id": 116,
      "start": 280.94,
      "end": 283.48,
      "en": "So would you really call this to someone, like to their face?",
      "zh": "那么你真的会把它叫给某人，喜欢当着他们的面吗？"
    },
    {
      "id": 117,
      "start": 283.92,
      "end": 284.06,
      "en": "No.",
      "zh": "不。"
    },
    {
      "id": 118,
      "start": 284.92,
      "end": 285.08,
      "en": "Definitely not.",
      "zh": "绝对不是。"
    },
    {
      "id": 119,
      "start": 285.92,
      "end": 286.48,
      "en": "It's definitely impolite.",
      "zh": "这绝对是不礼貌的。"
    },
    {
      "id": 120,
      "start": 286.92,
      "end": 287.92,
      "en": "Right.",
      "zh": "对。"
    },
    {
      "id": 121,
      "start": 287.92,
      "end": 289.32,
      "en": "You can't say to someone, oh, you're a nut job.",
      "zh": "你不能对某人说，哦，你是个疯子。"
    },
    {
      "id": 122,
      "start": 289.32,
      "end": 290.32,
      "en": "Yeah.",
      "zh": "对。"
    },
    {
      "id": 123,
      "start": 290.32,
      "end": 290.68,
      "en": "But it's not a swear word.",
      "zh": "但这不是一个脏话。"
    },
    {
      "id": 124,
      "start": 291.32,
      "end": 293.0,
      "en": "No, but it's a little bit insulting, right?",
      "zh": "不，但有点侮辱，对吧？"
    },
    {
      "id": 125,
      "start": 293.1,
      "end": 295.48,
      "en": "It's like saying you're crazy, but stronger.",
      "zh": "这就像说你疯了，但更强大。"
    },
    {
      "id": 126,
      "start": 295.98,
      "end": 297.2,
      "en": "Well, the doctor was a nut job.",
      "zh": "嗯，医生是个疯子。"
    },
    {
      "id": 127,
      "start": 297.58,
      "end": 302.24,
      "en": "He was stalking her and she apologized to Steven for getting him worked up.",
      "zh": "他在跟踪她，她向史蒂文道歉，因为他让他工作。"
    },
    {
      "id": 128,
      "start": 302.58,
      "end": 303.38,
      "en": "Worked up.",
      "zh": "工作了。"
    },
    {
      "id": 129,
      "start": 303.86,
      "end": 305.02,
      "en": "So work up.",
      "zh": "所以努力。"
    },
    {
      "id": 130,
      "start": 305.5,
      "end": 306.46,
      "en": "To be worked up.",
      "zh": "被激发。"
    },
    {
      "id": 131,
      "start": 306.82,
      "end": 308.44,
      "en": "When you get worked up, what happens?",
      "zh": "当你心烦意乱时，会发生什么？"
    },
    {
      "id": 132,
      "start": 309.12,
      "end": 315.8,
      "en": "You get really emotional and usually angry or sad or upset, but a negative emotion.",
      "zh": "你会变得非常情绪化，通常会生气、悲伤或沮丧，但会产生负面情绪。"
    },
    {
      "id": 133,
      "start": 316.36,
      "end": 316.54,
      "en": "Okay.",
      "zh": "好的。"
    },
    {
      "id": 134,
      "start": 316.54,
      "end": 318.16,
      "en": "So you got worked up.",
      "zh": "所以你被激怒了。"
    },
    {
      "id": 135,
      "start": 318.68,
      "end": 320.72,
      "en": "So it's always used with the verb to get.",
      "zh": "所以它总是与动词一起使用以获得。"
    },
    {
      "id": 136,
      "start": 321.12,
      "end": 322.16,
      "en": "So to get worked up.",
      "zh": "所以要努力。"
    },
    {
      "id": 137,
      "start": 322.36,
      "end": 322.5,
      "en": "Okay.",
      "zh": "好的。"
    },
    {
      "id": 138,
      "start": 323.36,
      "end": 323.58,
      "en": "You get worked up.",
      "zh": "你开始工作了。"
    },
    {
      "id": 139,
      "start": 324.36,
      "end": 324.66,
      "en": "You got worked up.",
      "zh": "你工作了。"
    },
    {
      "id": 140,
      "start": 325.36,
      "end": 326.36,
      "en": "Okay.",
      "zh": "好的。"
    },
    {
      "id": 141,
      "start": 326.36,
      "end": 327.36,
      "en": "Very good.",
      "zh": "很好。"
    },
    {
      "id": 142,
      "start": 327.36,
      "end": 329.94,
      "en": "And well, Stephen got worked up over nothing, but he didn't mind.",
      "zh": "好吧，斯蒂芬无缘无故地激怒了，但他并不介意。"
    },
    {
      "id": 143,
      "start": 329.94,
      "end": 334.5,
      "en": "He said she is his love and he called her his soulmate.",
      "zh": "他说她是他的爱人，他称她为他的灵魂伴侣。"
    },
    {
      "id": 144,
      "start": 334.92,
      "end": 335.76,
      "en": "His soulmate.",
      "zh": "他的灵魂伴侣。"
    },
    {
      "id": 145,
      "start": 336.32,
      "end": 336.84,
      "en": "Soulmate.",
      "zh": "灵魂伴侣。"
    },
    {
      "id": 146,
      "start": 337.4,
      "end": 337.62,
      "en": "That's right.",
      "zh": "没错。"
    },
    {
      "id": 147,
      "start": 337.92,
      "end": 342.63,
      "en": "That's a very romantic word, meaning the perfect person for you.",
      "zh": "这是一个非常浪漫的词，对你来说意味着完美的人。"
    },
    {
      "id": 148,
      "start": 342.92,
      "end": 343.92,
      "en": "Right.",
      "zh": "对。"
    },
    {
      "id": 149,
      "start": 343.92,
      "end": 344.92,
      "en": "Your other half.",
      "zh": "你的另一半。"
    },
    {
      "id": 150,
      "start": 344.92,
      "end": 345.92,
      "en": "Yes.",
      "zh": "是的。"
    },
    {
      "id": 151,
      "start": 345.92,
      "end": 346.92,
      "en": "Okay.",
      "zh": "好的。"
    },
    {
      "id": 152,
      "start": 346.92,
      "end": 348.88,
      "en": "So your soulmate is that perfect complement for you.",
      "zh": "所以你的灵魂伴侣是你的完美补充。"
    },
    {
      "id": 153,
      "start": 348.88,
      "end": 350.06,
      "en": "And it's usually romantic, right?",
      "zh": "而且通常很浪漫，对吧？"
    },
    {
      "id": 154,
      "start": 350.84,
      "end": 354.56,
      "en": "Usually romantic, but sometimes you might use it with your very, very, very best friend.",
      "zh": "通常是浪漫的，但有时你可能会和你非常、非常、非常好的朋友一起使用它。"
    },
    {
      "id": 155,
      "start": 354.96,
      "end": 355.12,
      "en": "Okay.",
      "zh": "好的。"
    },
    {
      "id": 156,
      "start": 355.96,
      "end": 357.02,
      "en": "Because you understand each other.",
      "zh": "因为你们互相理解。"
    },
    {
      "id": 157,
      "start": 357.44,
      "end": 358.44,
      "en": "Yeah.",
      "zh": "对。"
    },
    {
      "id": 158,
      "start": 358.44,
      "end": 359.36,
      "en": "You know what the other one's thinking.",
      "zh": "你知道对方在想什么。"
    },
    {
      "id": 159,
      "start": 359.7,
      "end": 360.92,
      "en": "You're the perfect fit together.",
      "zh": "你们是完美的搭配。"
    },
    {
      "id": 160,
      "start": 361.3,
      "end": 361.52,
      "en": "Okay.",
      "zh": "好的。"
    },
    {
      "id": 161,
      "start": 361.76,
      "end": 362.24,
      "en": "Soulmate.",
      "zh": "灵魂伴侣。"
    },
    {
      "id": 162,
      "start": 363.48,
      "end": 364.48,
      "en": "Very good.",
      "zh": "很好。"
    },
    {
      "id": 163,
      "start": 364.48,
      "end": 366.48,
      "en": "Well, we've seen some really interesting words.",
      "zh": "好吧，我们看到了一些非常有趣的词。"
    },
    {
      "id": 164,
      "start": 367.0,
      "end": 372.34,
      "en": "So why don't we listen to our dialogue again, and then we'll come back and look at some of the phrases that were used.",
      "zh": "那么我们为什么不再听我们的对话，然后我们会回来看看一些使用的短语。"
    },
    {
      "id": 165,
      "start": 378.28,
      "end": 379.62,
      "en": "Thank God you showed up when you did.",
      "zh": "谢天谢地，你来得正是时候。"
    },
    {
      "id": 166,
      "start": 380.52,
      "end": 380.66,
      "en": "He's insane.",
      "zh": "他疯了。"
    },
    {
      "id": 167,
      "start": 381.68,
      "end": 383.08,
      "en": "Do you think we should call the police?",
      "zh": "你认为我们应该报警吗？"
    },
    {
      "id": 168,
      "start": 383.8,
      "end": 384.78,
      "en": "Don't worry about it.",
      "zh": "别担心。"
    },
    {
      "id": 169,
      "start": 385.3,
      "end": 387.16,
      "en": "I'll call my friend and have him take care of it.",
      "zh": "我会找个朋友处理这事。"
    },
    {
      "id": 170,
      "start": 387.56,
      "end": 389.38,
      "en": "I can't believe he was stalking you all these years.",
      "zh": "真没想到他这些年一直在跟踪你。"
    },
    {
      "id": 171,
      "start": 389.62,
      "end": 390.26,
      "en": "What a nut job.",
      "zh": "真是个疯子。"
    },
    {
      "id": 172,
      "start": 390.6,
      "end": 391.18,
      "en": "I know.",
      "zh": "我知道。"
    },
    {
      "id": 173,
      "start": 391.82,
      "end": 393.64,
      "en": "Well, he said I'm not pregnant.",
      "zh": "好吧，他说我没有怀孕。"
    },
    {
      "id": 174,
      "start": 394.58,
      "end": 396.9,
      "en": "I'm sorry if I got you all worked up over nothing.",
      "zh": "对不起，让你为一场乌龙紧张成这样。"
    },
    {
      "id": 175,
      "start": 397.62,
      "end": 400.06,
      "en": "I want you to know that I didn't do it on purpose.",
      "zh": "你要知道，我不是故意的。"
    },
    {
      "id": 176,
      "start": 400.5,
      "end": 400.94,
      "en": "Don't apologize.",
      "zh": "不用道歉。"
    },
    {
      "id": 177,
      "start": 401.9,
      "end": 406.02,
      "en": "From the moment I met you, not a day has gone by when I haven't thought of you.",
      "zh": "自从认识你，我一天都没停止想你。"
    },
    {
      "id": 178,
      "start": 406.88,
      "end": 410.21,
      "en": "And now that I'm with you again, I'm just scared, Veronica.",
      "zh": "现在我又和你在一起了，我只是害怕，维罗妮卡。"
    },
    {
      "id": 179,
      "start": 410.8,
      "end": 412.35,
      "en": "The closer I get to you, the worse it gets.",
      "zh": "我越靠近你，就越害怕。"
    },
    {
      "id": 180,
      "start": 413.59,
      "end": 417.51,
      "en": "The thought of not being with you, I mean, I just can't handle it.",
      "zh": "我一想到可能失去你，就受不了。"
    },
    {
      "id": 181,
      "start": 417.95,
      "end": 419.37,
      "en": "We were made for each other, Veronica.",
      "zh": "维罗妮卡，我们是天生一对。"
    },
    {
      "id": 182,
      "start": 420.17,
      "end": 421.19,
      "en": "You're my everything.",
      "zh": "你是我的一切。"
    },
    {
      "id": 183,
      "start": 421.75,
      "end": 422.75,
      "en": "My soulmate.",
      "zh": "我的灵魂伴侣。"
    },
    {
      "id": 184,
      "start": 423.55,
      "end": 424.39,
      "en": "What can I do?",
      "zh": "我能怎么办？"
    },
    {
      "id": 185,
      "start": 424.81,
      "end": 425.75,
      "en": "Just hold me.",
      "zh": "抱紧我。"
    },
    {
      "id": 186,
      "start": 426.31,
      "end": 428.47,
      "en": "I'll always be here for you, no matter what.",
      "zh": "无论如何，我都会一直在你身边。"
    },
    {
      "id": 187,
      "start": 429.21,
      "end": 432.79,
      "en": "And together, we can tackle whatever life throws at us.",
      "zh": "不管生活带来什么难题，我们都能一起面对。"
    },
    {
      "id": 188,
      "start": 433.39,
      "end": 434.65,
      "en": "I believe in us, Steven.",
      "zh": "我相信我们，史蒂文。"
    },
    {
      "id": 189,
      "start": 435.69,
      "end": 437.09,
      "en": "I'm so happy to hear that.",
      "zh": "我很高兴听到这个消息。"
    },
    {
      "id": 190,
      "start": 437.53,
      "end": 438.91,
      "en": "I know we belong together.",
      "zh": "我知道我们注定在一起。"
    },
    {
      "id": 191,
      "start": 439.98,
      "end": 440.78,
      "en": "I love you so much.",
      "zh": "我非常爱你。"
    },
    {
      "id": 192,
      "start": 445.13,
      "end": 453.87,
      "en": "That was a little bit more clear this time, but now I want to look at some phrases in the dialogue and see how they can be put together.",
      "zh": "这次更清楚一点，但现在我想看看对话中的一些短语，看看如何将它们放在一起。"
    },
    {
      "id": 193,
      "start": 456.05,
      "end": 456.93,
      "en": "Putting it together.",
      "zh": "综合运用。"
    },
    {
      "id": 194,
      "start": 458.29,
      "end": 464.27,
      "en": "So Veronica apologized to Steven for getting him worked up over nothing.",
      "zh": "所以维罗妮卡向史蒂文道歉，因为他让他无所事事。"
    },
    {
      "id": 195,
      "start": 464.88,
      "end": 465.11,
      "en": "Over nothing.",
      "zh": "无所事事。"
    },
    {
      "id": 196,
      "start": 465.88,
      "end": 466.01,
      "en": "Over nothing.",
      "zh": "无所事事。"
    },
    {
      "id": 197,
      "start": 466.88,
      "end": 467.93,
      "en": "Now it's the complete sentence.",
      "zh": "现在是完整的句子。"
    },
    {
      "id": 198,
      "start": 468.47,
      "end": 471.43,
      "en": "I'm sorry for getting you worked up over nothing.",
      "zh": "我很抱歉让你因为什么都没有而烦恼。"
    },
    {
      "id": 199,
      "start": 471.75,
      "end": 474.37,
      "en": "So over nothing means for no reason, right?",
      "zh": "所以没有任何意义，对吧？"
    },
    {
      "id": 200,
      "start": 474.47,
      "end": 475.01,
      "en": "Right, exactly.",
      "zh": "对，没错。"
    },
    {
      "id": 201,
      "start": 475.53,
      "end": 479.85,
      "en": "So why don't we listen to some other examples of how we can use over nothing.",
      "zh": "那么我们为什么不听一些其他例子来说明我们如何使用无所事事。"
    },
    {
      "id": 202,
      "start": 480.99,
      "end": 481.91,
      "en": "Example one.",
      "zh": "例句一。"
    },
    {
      "id": 203,
      "start": 484.16,
      "end": 486.44,
      "en": "You always get angry over nothing.",
      "zh": "你总是因为无所事事而生气。"
    },
    {
      "id": 204,
      "start": 486.96,
      "end": 488.48,
      "en": "You have such a bad temper.",
      "zh": "你的脾气真坏。"
    },
    {
      "id": 205,
      "start": 491.64,
      "end": 491.92,
      "en": "Example two.",
      "zh": "例句二。"
    },
    {
      "id": 206,
      "start": 495.32,
      "end": 496.88,
      "en": "I called the police last night over nothing.",
      "zh": "昨晚我报了警，无缘无故。"
    },
    {
      "id": 207,
      "start": 497.6,
      "end": 498.9,
      "en": "I thought I had a thief in my house.",
      "zh": "我以为我家里有小偷。"
    },
    {
      "id": 208,
      "start": 501.58,
      "end": 502.7,
      "en": "Example three.",
      "zh": "例句三。"
    },
    {
      "id": 209,
      "start": 505.27,
      "end": 506.35,
      "en": "Let's not fight over nothing.",
      "zh": "让我们不要为任何事情而战。"
    },
    {
      "id": 210,
      "start": 506.83,
      "end": 507.93,
      "en": "Let's just have dinner in peace.",
      "zh": "让我们平静地吃晚饭。"
    },
    {
      "id": 211,
      "start": 510.72,
      "end": 514.92,
      "en": "Okay so we see you can use many different verbs together with over nothing.",
      "zh": "好的，我们看到您可以将许多不同的动词一起使用，但没有。"
    },
    {
      "id": 212,
      "start": 515.38,
      "end": 520.56,
      "en": "So get excited over nothing, get angry over nothing, get upset over nothing.",
      "zh": "所以因为什么都没有而兴奋，因为什么都没有生气，对什么都没有生气。"
    },
    {
      "id": 213,
      "start": 520.86,
      "end": 521.02,
      "en": "Exactly.",
      "zh": "正是这样。"
    },
    {
      "id": 214,
      "start": 522.16,
      "end": 522.62,
      "en": "Very good.",
      "zh": "很好。"
    },
    {
      "id": 215,
      "start": 523.16,
      "end": 523.52,
      "en": "So over nothing.",
      "zh": "所以什么都没有。"
    },
    {
      "id": 216,
      "start": 524.58,
      "end": 525.62,
      "en": "And now for our next phrase.",
      "zh": "现在是我们的下一个短语。"
    },
    {
      "id": 217,
      "start": 526.14,
      "end": 534.84,
      "en": "So when Steven was telling Veronica how much he loved her, he told her, not a day has gone by when I haven't thought of you.",
      "zh": "所以当史蒂文告诉维罗妮卡他有多爱她时，他告诉她，没有一天我没有想到你。"
    },
    {
      "id": 218,
      "start": 534.84,
      "end": 536.72,
      "en": "So not a day has gone by.",
      "zh": "所以没有一天过去了。"
    },
    {
      "id": 219,
      "start": 537.96,
      "end": 541.62,
      "en": "So that part of the sentence, not a day has gone by, what does he mean by that?",
      "zh": "所以那部分句子，没有一天过去了，他是什么意思？"
    },
    {
      "id": 220,
      "start": 542.2,
      "end": 544.88,
      "en": "He means basically every day I think of you.",
      "zh": "他的意思是基本上每天我都在想你。"
    },
    {
      "id": 221,
      "start": 545.64,
      "end": 548.13,
      "en": "There hasn't been a moment where I haven't thought of you.",
      "zh": "没有一刻我没有想到你。"
    },
    {
      "id": 222,
      "start": 548.6,
      "end": 550.15,
      "en": "Now how can we change it a little bit?",
      "zh": "现在我们如何改变它一点？"
    },
    {
      "id": 223,
      "start": 550.32,
      "end": 551.65,
      "en": "What can we change within this phrase?",
      "zh": "我们可以在这句话中改变什么？"
    },
    {
      "id": 224,
      "start": 552.03,
      "end": 553.69,
      "en": "Well, you can put in different times.",
      "zh": "好吧，你可以放在不同的时间。"
    },
    {
      "id": 225,
      "start": 554.55,
      "end": 559.95,
      "en": "So not a day has gone by, not an hour has gone by, not a moment has gone by.",
      "zh": "所以没有一天过去了，没有一个小时过去了，没有一个时刻过去了。"
    },
    {
      "id": 226,
      "start": 560.33,
      "end": 561.91,
      "en": "Not a month, not a year.",
      "zh": "不是一个月，不是一年。"
    },
    {
      "id": 227,
      "start": 562.33,
      "end": 562.63,
      "en": "Exactly.",
      "zh": "正是这样。"
    },
    {
      "id": 228,
      "start": 563.84,
      "end": 566.0,
      "en": "So you can use different times in that phrase.",
      "zh": "因此，您可以在该短语中使用不同的时间。"
    },
    {
      "id": 229,
      "start": 566.0,
      "end": 570.56,
      "en": "But an important thing is that the complement is always negative, right?",
      "zh": "但重要的是，补码总是消极的，对吧？"
    },
    {
      "id": 230,
      "start": 570.88,
      "end": 571.88,
      "en": "That's right.",
      "zh": "没错。"
    },
    {
      "id": 231,
      "start": 571.88,
      "end": 572.78,
      "en": "So it's always followed by a negative.",
      "zh": "所以它总是跟着一个否定。"
    },
    {
      "id": 232,
      "start": 573.54,
      "end": 577.3,
      "en": "Not a day has gone by that I haven't wished you were here.",
      "zh": "没有一天，我不希望你在这里。"
    },
    {
      "id": 233,
      "start": 577.96,
      "end": 579.12,
      "en": "So it's followed by a negative.",
      "zh": "所以它后面是一个负面的。"
    },
    {
      "id": 234,
      "start": 579.62,
      "end": 579.98,
      "en": "That's right.",
      "zh": "没错。"
    },
    {
      "id": 235,
      "start": 580.54,
      "end": 581.38,
      "en": "Maybe one more.",
      "zh": "或许再来一份。"
    },
    {
      "id": 236,
      "start": 582.06,
      "end": 585.84,
      "en": "Not a second has gone by that I haven't missed you.",
      "zh": "没有一秒钟，我没有想念你。"
    },
    {
      "id": 237,
      "start": 587.12,
      "end": 588.12,
      "en": "Very good examples.",
      "zh": "非常好的例子。"
    },
    {
      "id": 238,
      "start": 588.12,
      "end": 589.12,
      "en": "Very romantic.",
      "zh": "真浪漫。"
    },
    {
      "id": 239,
      "start": 589.12,
      "end": 589.36,
      "en": "Oh Marco.",
      "zh": "哦马可。"
    },
    {
      "id": 240,
      "start": 590.12,
      "end": 591.12,
      "en": "Yeah.",
      "zh": "对。"
    },
    {
      "id": 241,
      "start": 591.12,
      "end": 592.12,
      "en": "All right.",
      "zh": "好的。"
    },
    {
      "id": 242,
      "start": 592.12,
      "end": 592.86,
      "en": "And now our last phrase.",
      "zh": "现在是我们的最后一句话。"
    },
    {
      "id": 243,
      "start": 593.4,
      "end": 597.11,
      "en": "He told her I'll always be here for you no matter what.",
      "zh": "他告诉她，无论如何我都会一直在你身边。"
    },
    {
      "id": 244,
      "start": 597.58,
      "end": 598.31,
      "en": "No matter what.",
      "zh": "无论如何。"
    },
    {
      "id": 245,
      "start": 599.04,
      "end": 599.65,
      "en": "No matter what.",
      "zh": "无论如何。"
    },
    {
      "id": 246,
      "start": 600.04,
      "end": 600.53,
      "en": "No matter what.",
      "zh": "无论如何。"
    },
    {
      "id": 247,
      "start": 601.04,
      "end": 601.53,
      "en": "What does he mean by that?",
      "zh": "他是什么意思？"
    },
    {
      "id": 248,
      "start": 602.04,
      "end": 605.81,
      "en": "Well, regardless of or you know, nothing's going to stop me.",
      "zh": "好吧，不管或者你知道，没有什么能阻止我。"
    },
    {
      "id": 249,
      "start": 606.16,
      "end": 606.31,
      "en": "Okay.",
      "zh": "好的。"
    },
    {
      "id": 250,
      "start": 606.35,
      "end": 611.09,
      "en": "So if I want to get that job, I'm going to get it no matter what.",
      "zh": "所以如果我想得到那份工作，无论如何我都会得到它。"
    },
    {
      "id": 251,
      "start": 611.29,
      "end": 612.37,
      "en": "So nothing's going to stop you.",
      "zh": "所以没有什么能阻止你。"
    },
    {
      "id": 252,
      "start": 612.67,
      "end": 616.45,
      "en": "Now we can change the WH word, what, at the end, right?",
      "zh": "现在我们可以改变 WH 字，到底是什么，对吧？"
    },
    {
      "id": 253,
      "start": 616.76,
      "end": 617.76,
      "en": "Yeah.",
      "zh": "对。"
    },
    {
      "id": 254,
      "start": 617.76,
      "end": 618.76,
      "en": "With other ones.",
      "zh": "与其他人。"
    },
    {
      "id": 255,
      "start": 618.76,
      "end": 619.76,
      "en": "Exactly.",
      "zh": "正是这样。"
    },
    {
      "id": 256,
      "start": 619.76,
      "end": 622.32,
      "en": "So, no matter where you are, I will find you.",
      "zh": "所以，无论你在哪里，我都会找到你。"
    },
    {
      "id": 257,
      "start": 622.32,
      "end": 623.32,
      "en": "Yeah.",
      "zh": "对。"
    },
    {
      "id": 258,
      "start": 623.32,
      "end": 624.32,
      "en": "No matter when.",
      "zh": "不管什么时候。"
    },
    {
      "id": 259,
      "start": 624.32,
      "end": 626.82,
      "en": "No matter when your birthday is, I will be there.",
      "zh": "不管你什么时候生日，我都会在那里。"
    },
    {
      "id": 260,
      "start": 627.32,
      "end": 628.32,
      "en": "That's right.",
      "zh": "没错。"
    },
    {
      "id": 261,
      "start": 628.32,
      "end": 631.08,
      "en": "You can see how you can use different WH words here.",
      "zh": "您可以在这里看到如何使用不同的 WH 词。"
    },
    {
      "id": 262,
      "start": 631.48,
      "end": 631.76,
      "en": "Okay.",
      "zh": "好的。"
    },
    {
      "id": 263,
      "start": 632.48,
      "end": 633.48,
      "en": "Very good.",
      "zh": "很好。"
    },
    {
      "id": 264,
      "start": 633.48,
      "end": 634.5,
      "en": "And it's a very common phrase, right?",
      "zh": "这是一个很常见的短语，对吧？"
    },
    {
      "id": 265,
      "start": 634.84,
      "end": 635.84,
      "en": "No matter what.",
      "zh": "无论如何。"
    },
    {
      "id": 266,
      "start": 635.84,
      "end": 636.22,
      "en": "No matter where.",
      "zh": "无论在哪里。"
    },
    {
      "id": 267,
      "start": 636.84,
      "end": 637.12,
      "en": "No matter when.",
      "zh": "不管什么时候。"
    },
    {
      "id": 268,
      "start": 637.84,
      "end": 638.06,
      "en": "No matter why.",
      "zh": "不管为什么。"
    },
    {
      "id": 269,
      "start": 638.84,
      "end": 639.84,
      "en": "No matter how.",
      "zh": "无论如何。"
    },
    {
      "id": 270,
      "start": 639.84,
      "end": 640.84,
      "en": "Yeah.",
      "zh": "对。"
    },
    {
      "id": 271,
      "start": 640.84,
      "end": 641.84,
      "en": "No matter how.",
      "zh": "无论如何。"
    },
    {
      "id": 272,
      "start": 641.84,
      "end": 642.84,
      "en": "Okay.",
      "zh": "好的。"
    },
    {
      "id": 273,
      "start": 642.84,
      "end": 649.0,
      "en": "So those were some really great phrases and I think you can play with them a little bit, change some things and then you can use them in your everyday life.",
      "zh": "所以这些是一些非常棒的短语，我认为你可以和它们一起玩，改变一些东西，然后你可以在你的日常生活中使用它们。"
    },
    {
      "id": 274,
      "start": 649.0,
      "end": 650.0,
      "en": "Right.",
      "zh": "对。"
    },
    {
      "id": 275,
      "start": 650.0,
      "end": 653.28,
      "en": "But why don't we hear them again one more time in context with the dialogue.",
      "zh": "但是，我们为什么不在对话的背景下再一次听到他们的声音。"
    },
    {
      "id": 276,
      "start": 663.0,
      "end": 664.34,
      "en": "Thank God you showed up when you did.",
      "zh": "谢天谢地，你来得正是时候。"
    },
    {
      "id": 277,
      "start": 665.24,
      "end": 665.48,
      "en": "He's insane.",
      "zh": "他疯了。"
    },
    {
      "id": 278,
      "start": 666.64,
      "end": 667.8,
      "en": "Do you think we should call the police?",
      "zh": "你认为我们应该报警吗？"
    },
    {
      "id": 279,
      "start": 668.56,
      "end": 669.52,
      "en": "Don't worry about it.",
      "zh": "别担心。"
    },
    {
      "id": 280,
      "start": 670.0,
      "end": 671.86,
      "en": "I'll call my friend and have him take care of it.",
      "zh": "我会找个朋友处理这事。"
    },
    {
      "id": 281,
      "start": 672.26,
      "end": 674.1,
      "en": "I can't believe he was stalking you all these years.",
      "zh": "真没想到他这些年一直在跟踪你。"
    },
    {
      "id": 282,
      "start": 674.4,
      "end": 675.4,
      "en": "What a nut job.",
      "zh": "真是个疯子。"
    },
    {
      "id": 283,
      "start": 675.4,
      "end": 675.84,
      "en": "I know.",
      "zh": "我知道。"
    },
    {
      "id": 284,
      "start": 676.56,
      "end": 678.36,
      "en": "Well, he said I'm not pregnant.",
      "zh": "好吧，他说我没有怀孕。"
    },
    {
      "id": 285,
      "start": 679.0,
      "end": 681.2,
      "en": "I'm sorry if I got you all worked up over nothing.",
      "zh": "对不起，让你为一场乌龙紧张成这样。"
    },
    {
      "id": 286,
      "start": 682.16,
      "end": 684.48,
      "en": "I want you to know that I didn't do it on purpose.",
      "zh": "你要知道，我不是故意的。"
    },
    {
      "id": 287,
      "start": 685.08,
      "end": 685.34,
      "en": "Don't apologize.",
      "zh": "不用道歉。"
    },
    {
      "id": 288,
      "start": 686.76,
      "end": 690.4,
      "en": "From the moment I met you, not a day has gone by when I haven't thought of you.",
      "zh": "自从认识你，我一天都没停止想你。"
    },
    {
      "id": 289,
      "start": 691.28,
      "end": 694.84,
      "en": "And now that I'm with you again, I'm just scared, Veronica.",
      "zh": "现在我又和你在一起了，我只是害怕，维罗妮卡。"
    },
    {
      "id": 290,
      "start": 695.46,
      "end": 697.0,
      "en": "The closer I get to you, the worse it gets.",
      "zh": "我越靠近你，就越害怕。"
    },
    {
      "id": 291,
      "start": 698.22,
      "end": 702.1,
      "en": "The thought of not being with you, I mean, I just can't handle it.",
      "zh": "我一想到可能失去你，就受不了。"
    },
    {
      "id": 292,
      "start": 702.6,
      "end": 703.94,
      "en": "We were made for each other, Veronica.",
      "zh": "维罗妮卡，我们是天生一对。"
    },
    {
      "id": 293,
      "start": 704.92,
      "end": 707.36,
      "en": "You're my everything, my soulmate.",
      "zh": "你是我的一切，我的灵魂伴侣。"
    },
    {
      "id": 294,
      "start": 707.86,
      "end": 709.02,
      "en": "What can I do?",
      "zh": "我能怎么办？"
    },
    {
      "id": 295,
      "start": 709.52,
      "end": 710.4,
      "en": "Just hold me.",
      "zh": "抱紧我。"
    },
    {
      "id": 296,
      "start": 710.98,
      "end": 713.1,
      "en": "I'll always be here for you, no matter what.",
      "zh": "无论如何，我都会一直在你身边。"
    },
    {
      "id": 297,
      "start": 713.86,
      "end": 717.46,
      "en": "And together, we can tackle whatever life throws at us.",
      "zh": "不管生活带来什么难题，我们都能一起面对。"
    },
    {
      "id": 298,
      "start": 718.04,
      "end": 719.32,
      "en": "I believe in us, Steven.",
      "zh": "我相信我们，史蒂文。"
    },
    {
      "id": 299,
      "start": 720.62,
      "end": 721.72,
      "en": "I'm so happy to hear that.",
      "zh": "我很高兴听到这个消息。"
    },
    {
      "id": 300,
      "start": 722.2,
      "end": 723.5,
      "en": "I know we belong together.",
      "zh": "我知道我们注定在一起。"
    },
    {
      "id": 301,
      "start": 723.6,
      "end": 724.6,
      "en": "I love you so much.",
      "zh": "我非常爱你。"
    },
    {
      "id": 302,
      "start": 724.67,
      "end": 725.41,
      "en": "I love you so much.",
      "zh": "我非常爱你。"
    },
    {
      "id": 303,
      "start": 745.4,
      "end": 747.24,
      "en": "Okay Erika, so who do you think got shot?",
      "zh": "好吧，埃里卡，你认为谁被枪杀了？"
    },
    {
      "id": 304,
      "start": 747.84,
      "end": 751.6,
      "en": "I don't know, but I'm starting to think this story is becoming a soap opera.",
      "zh": "我不知道，但我开始认为这个故事正在成为一部肥皂剧。"
    },
    {
      "id": 305,
      "start": 752.36,
      "end": 757.52,
      "en": "Well, it certainly is and well, what do you guys think happened or who do you think got shot or?",
      "zh": "好吧，它当然是，好吧，你们认为发生了什么，或者你认为谁被枪杀了？"
    },
    {
      "id": 306,
      "start": 757.52,
      "end": 758.52,
      "en": "Who did the shooting?",
      "zh": "拍摄的是谁？"
    },
    {
      "id": 307,
      "start": 758.6,
      "end": 759.2,
      "en": "Who shot who?",
      "zh": "谁拍的是谁？"
    },
    {
      "id": 308,
      "start": 759.66,
      "end": 760.06,
      "en": "Maybe...",
      "zh": "也许..."
    },
    {
      "id": 309,
      "start": 760.52,
      "end": 761.52,
      "en": "Was it even a gunshot?",
      "zh": "甚至是枪声吗？"
    },
    {
      "id": 310,
      "start": 761.52,
      "end": 763.88,
      "en": "Maybe it was just the car.",
      "zh": "也许这只是汽车。"
    },
    {
      "id": 311,
      "start": 763.88,
      "end": 764.8,
      "en": "The tire could have popped.",
      "zh": "轮胎可能已经爆裂。"
    },
    {
      "id": 312,
      "start": 765.1,
      "end": 765.4,
      "en": "I don't know.",
      "zh": "我不知道。"
    },
    {
      "id": 313,
      "start": 766.0,
      "end": 767.0,
      "en": "Exactly.",
      "zh": "正是这样。"
    },
    {
      "id": 314,
      "start": 767.0,
      "end": 778.68,
      "en": "So well, come to our website, tell us what you think happens or what you would like to happen because I know many people are expecting a little bit more romance maybe and less drama.",
      "zh": "好吧，来我们的网站，告诉我们你的想法或你想发生什么，因为我知道很多人期待更多的浪漫和更少的戏剧性。"
    },
    {
      "id": 315,
      "start": 778.68,
      "end": 782.88,
      "en": "But if you have any questions about the language in this lesson, please visit the website at EnglishPod.com.",
      "zh": "但是，如果您对本课程中的语言有任何疑问，请访问 englishpod.com 的网站。"
    },
    {
      "id": 316,
      "start": 783.14,
      "end": 783.56,
      "en": "Exactly.",
      "zh": "正是这样。"
    },
    {
      "id": 317,
      "start": 783.98,
      "end": 788.18,
      "en": "Erica and I are always there to answer your questions and well, anything you guys need.",
      "zh": "埃里卡和我总是在那里回答你的问题，好吧，你们需要的任何东西。"
    },
    {
      "id": 318,
      "start": 788.88,
      "end": 789.88,
      "en": "Anything?",
      "zh": "有什么吗？"
    },
    {
      "id": 319,
      "start": 789.88,
      "end": 790.88,
      "en": "Anything.",
      "zh": "任何东西。"
    },
    {
      "id": 320,
      "start": 790.88,
      "end": 793.88,
      "en": "Well, thanks for listening to this lesson and until next time, goodbye.",
      "zh": "好吧，感谢您收听本课，直到下一次，再见。"
    },
    {
      "id": 321,
      "start": 793.88,
      "end": 803.265,
      "en": "Bye!",
      "zh": "再见！"
    }
